            "review_title": "Review at A Mà Kitchen",
            "review_text": "Manuel D\n120 contributions\n0\nTasty and a bit pricier\nDec 2025 • Couples\nWe chose this restaurant because it seemed to be packed everyday.\n\nThe restaurant is beautifully decorated. No matter where you look you will find something beautiful. \n\nThe menu offers a wide variety of chinese cuisine. It is even possible to get a whole crispy peking duck and get it cut right in front of you.\nAfter getting a small led tablet and a sheet of paper we chose what we wanted for our dinner.\n\nWe got steamed custard buns, soup dumplings, rips with beancurd and a boiling hot stonepot filled with minced pork, mushrooms and aubergine. Drink wise you have many different teas to chose from which made it obvious that we had to give it a try. The teas did not disappoint.\n\nSadly though many dishes that we preselected while looking online for the restaurant at home were already sold out. Therefor i have to deduct a star.\nRead more\nWritten December 1, 2025",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-15",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
